**Source** (`prelude.cljc`)
- Both `integer/compare` endpoint clauses **removed** from `php/obj-val?`; `integer/add`/`integer/sub` and `integer/integer?` preserved untouched; `host-names` and `php/finalize!` not touched (Ruling 3).
- Replaced with a **limit-aware probe**, not a bare revert, per re-check5's explicit warning:
  ```clojure
  (if (integer/integer? rc)
    (if (integer/integer? (integer/add rc 1))     ; addref's own operation
      (integer/integer? (integer/add rc rc))      ; a bit of headroom under ::max-bits
      false) false)
  ```
  The doubling answers sol's correction (2) — an admission-time bound is a snapshot, because counts grow by one per acquisition. With headroom, crossing the limit needs ≥2^(max-bits−1) acquisitions, while MAX/MIN/2^63/BigInt carriers all stay LOCAL (65 bits ≪ 4096).

